 That was the first decline in three years, after +3.1% in Q4 2025 and +1.8% in Q1 2026. Shipments trail orders by about two quarters, so the weakness should carry into late 2026 and 2027.\n- **Voltaris:** Its shipments fell 9% in Q2, the steepest among large makers. Its market share dropped from 31% to 27%, with Tarnwell and imports gaining.\n- **Revenue:** Quarterly revenue was C$905M, C$960M, C$980M and C$890M from Q3 2025 to Q2 2026. That is about C$3.7B over the last four quarters, and Q2 was down 9% from Q1.\n\n**What it implies for 2027**\n- **Run rate:** Holding Q2's C$890M flat gives about C$3.56B for 2027. Returning to the C$3.7B trailing level gives about C$3.7B.\n- **Reaching C$4.2B:** That needs roughly 13–18% growth over the run rate. It would take a rebound in industry shipments and recovery of the lost share.\n- **Share sensitivity:** If the industry grows 3% and Voltaris holds 27% share, revenue would be about C$3.6–3.8B. Winning back to 31% share would be about 15% more, which lands near C$4.2B. That makes guidance a share-recovery bet.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The data covers one industry quarter and four company quarters.\n- I assumed revenue tracks shipments. Pricing and mix could add upside that this data can't show.\n- I did not look at backlog or orders. That is n2's question.","ttft_ms":2395,"type":"result","duration_ms":19448,"uuid":"165c9ad5-cf04-49ad-82aa-77fd25a441ae","ttft_stream_ms":1218,"time_to_request_ms":364,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":25,"system_prompt":23,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":14,"input_attachments":75,"input_hooks":16,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":12,"init_message":30,"init_frame_send":15,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":15,"message_prep":13,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":13,"request_announcements":29,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":9,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":15,"client_creation":15,"request_build":26},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index